      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-16174",
      ":question/problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are twice-differentiable on an open interval containing $x = 10$. The values of $f$, $g$, and their respective derivatives are given below:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $f^{\u2032}(x)$ | $f^{\u2033}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $g^{\u2032}(x)$ | $g^{\u2033}(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $10$ | $-5$ | $0$ | $3$ | $-20$ | $-2$ | $-6$ |\n\nFind $lim_(x \u2192 10)(f(x) + 5)/(2x + g(x))$."
