      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-16175",
      ":question/problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are twice-differentiable on an open interval containing $x = 0$. The values of $f$, $g$, and their respective derivatives are given below:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $f^{\u2032}(x)$ | $f^{\u2033}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $g^{\u2032}(x)$ | $g^{\u2033}(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\nFind $lim_(x \u2192 0)(e^{x} - f(x))/(x^{2} + g(x))$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186234323,
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72361",
      ":question/problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are twice-differentiable on an open interval containing $x=1.$ The values of $f,$ $g,$ and their respective derivatives are given below:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{'}(x)$ | ${f}^{''}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{'}(x)$ | ${g}^{''}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{f(x)+x}{g(x)-x}.$"
    }
